===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A place at which one is regularly found; a [[habitation]] or [[hangout]].
#: {{syn|en|repair}}
#: {{ux|en|The shopping mall is a popular '''haunt''' of the local teenagers in this town.}}
#: {{ux|en|I went back the town I used to live and visited all my old '''haunts'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1868|author=w:Louisa May Alcott|title=Kitty's Class Day
|passage=Both Jack and Fletcher had graduated the year before, but still took an interest in their old '''haunts''', and patronized the fellows who were not yet through.}}
#* {{RQ:Time|date=8 Oct 1984|author=Timothy Loughran; Natalie Angier|title=Science: Striking It Rich in Wyoming|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20101029143953/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,955334,00.html
|passage=Wyoming has been a favorite '''haunt''' of paleontologists for the past century ever since westering pioneers reported that many vertebrate fossils were almost lying on the ground.}}
# {{lb|en|dialect}} A [[ghost]].
#: {{syn|en|haint}}
# A lair or feeding place of animals in the wild.
#: {{hyper|en|colony}}
#: {{hypo|en|burrow|den|earth|hive|nest|warren}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1769|author={{w|Firishta}}|tlr={{w|Alexander Dow}}|title=Tales translated from the Persian of Inatulla of Delhi|volume=I|publisher=P. and W. Wilson et al.|location=Dublin|page=iv|text=The lofty mountains roſe faint to the ſight and loſt their foreheads in the diſtant ſkies: the little hills, cloathed in darker green and ſkirted with embroidered vales, diſcovered the ſecret '''haunts''' of kids and bounding roes.}}

